        &#9989; = a register block is described in this addrmap; &#10060; = not described (reserved, memory window, or media/ISP/security block outside the bring-up scope). The address table is the data sheet's Table 1-4 (the on-chip RAM/BOOTROM remark of the 0x00000000 row and the DDR size remark of the 0x80000000 row are restored from the data sheet text). This file and `hi3518ev200.rdl` carry the same table and instance list: change both.

        <!-- overview:begin -->

        ### Diagrams

        ![Logic block diagram](assets/diagrams/hi3516cv200-logic.svg)

        ![Register blocks by function](assets/diagrams/hi3516cv200-blocks.svg)

