        ![Bus masters and DDR QoS groups](assets/diagrams/hi3516cv200-busqos.svg)

        ![Power domains](assets/diagrams/hi3516cv200-power.svg)

        ![CRG register map](assets/diagrams/hi3516cv200-crgmap.svg)

        ![IP editions across the camera family](assets/diagrams/hi3516cv200-editions.svg)

        ### Pass-2 additions (2026-11-15)

        The Hi3518E V200 / V201 / Hi3516C V200 root descriptions above already carry the variants table, the boot description, the interrupt table and the facts list; the additions below are the DMA lines, pin multiplexing, clocks, reset/power, bus ports and the extra diagrams.

        ### Camera family comparison (data sheet chapter 1)

        One column per chip, taken from the data sheets named in the header row below; `-` = the sheet gives no value. The Hi3518 sheet covers the A and C variants; the Hi3518E V200 sheet covers V200, V201 and Hi3516C V200.

        | Item | Hi3516 V100 | Hi3516C V100 | Hi3518A V100 | Hi3518C V100 | Hi3518E V100 | Hi3516C V300 | Hi3516E V100 | Hi3518E V200 | Hi3518E V201 | Hi3516C V200 |
        |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
        | Data sheet (issue, date, language) | 00B60 2011-08-12, Chinese | 00B02 2013-02-05 | Hi3518 sheet (A and C in one document) | same document as A | 03 2015-11-26 | 05 2018-05-10 (C V300 and E V100 in one document) | same document as C V300 | 02 2017-06-12 (one document for V200, V201, Hi3516C V200) | same document | same document |
        | CPU | Cortex-A9 up to 800 MHz, VFP, 32 KB I + 32 KB D L1, 256 KB L2, about 2000 DMIPS | ARM926 up to 440 MHz, 16 KB I + 16 KB D, 2 KB ITCM | ARM926 up to 440 MHz, 16 KB I + 16 KB D, 2 KB ITCM | ARM926 up to 440 MHz, 16 KB I + 16 KB D, 2 KB ITCM | ARM926 up to 440 MHz, 16 KB I + 16 KB D | ARM926 up to 800 MHz, 32 KB I + 32 KB D | ARM926 up to 800 MHz, 32 KB I + 32 KB D | ARM926 540 MHz, 32 KB I + 32 KB D | ARM926 540 MHz, 32 KB I + 32 KB D | ARM926 600 MHz, 32 KB I + 32 KB D |
        | Interrupt controller | ARM GIC (A9 MPCore), IDs 0-31 internal | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC |
        | DDR | DDR2/DDR3, 32 or 16 bit, up to 500 MHz, 1 GB (32 bit) / 512 MB (16 bit) | DDR2/DDR3, 16 bit, up to 440 MHz, up to 256 MB | DDR2/DDR3, 16 bit, up to 400 MHz, up to 256 MB | DDR2/DDR3, 16 bit, up to 400 MHz, up to 128 MB | embedded 16-bit DDR2, up to 512 Mbit | external 16-bit DDR3/DDR3L, up to 4 Gbit | embedded 512 Mbit DDR (1.8 V) | embedded 16-bit DDR2 512 Mbit, 360 MHz | embedded 16-bit DDR2 256 Mbit, 360 MHz | external 16-bit DDR2/DDR3/DDR3L, up to 4 Gbit, 400 MHz |
        | Boot media | NAND, SPI flash, or PCIe load into DDR | SPI NOR, NAND | SPI NOR, NAND | SPI NOR only | SPI NOR only | SPI NOR/NAND, eMMC (4-bit), serial (fastboot), SD/USB update | same as C V300 (SPI NOR/NAND, eMMC, fastboot, update) | serial (BOOTROM), SPI NOR/NAND, eMMC | same as V200 | same as V200 |
        | Flash controllers | NANDC (2 CS), SFC (2 CS) | SFC (1 CS), NANDC | SFC (1 CS), NANDC | SFC (1 CS) | SFC (1 CS) | FMC (SPI NOR/NAND), eMMC via MMC | FMC, eMMC via MMC | FMC, eMMC | FMC, eMMC | FMC, eMMC |
        | Video encoder | H.264 BP/MP/HP, MPEG4 SP, JPEG; up to 16 Mpixel | H.264 BP/MP, MJPEG/JPEG; 1080p@30 + VGA@30 + JPEG 1080p@1 | H.264 BP/MP, MJPEG/JPEG; 720p@30 + VGA@30 + QVGA@30 + JPEG 720p@1 | H.264 BP/MP, MJPEG/JPEG; 720p@30 + QVGA@30 + JPEG 720p@1 | H.264 BP/MP, MJPEG/JPEG; 720p@25 + JPEG 720p@3 | H.264 BP/MP/HP, H.265 Main, MJPEG/JPEG; 2048x2048@15 + 640x640@15, or 1080p@30 + 480p@30 + 240p@30 | same codecs; 1536x1536 (width up to 2048); 1080p@20 + 576p@20 | H.264 BP/MP/HP, MJPEG/JPEG; 1080p@20 | H.264 BP/MP/HP, MJPEG/JPEG; 960p@25 (no LDC, no 90/270 rotation) | H.264 BP/MP/HP, MJPEG/JPEG; 1080p@30 |
        | Video in | 8-16 bit RGB Bayer up to 150 MHz, BT.601/656/1120, dual sensor | 8/10/12-bit Bayer up to 74.25 MHz, BT.656/BT.1120 | 8/10/12-bit Bayer up to 74.25 MHz, BT.656/BT.1120 | 8/10/12-bit Bayer up to 74.25 MHz, BT.656/BT.1120 | 8/10/12-bit Bayer up to 74.25 MHz, BT.656/BT.1120, 1080p@30 / 720p@30 | 8-14 bit Bayer DC, BT.601/656/1120, MIPI, LVDS/sub-LVDS, HiSPi, up to 2048x2048 and 250 Mpixel/s | same as C V300 | MIPI / LVDS / HiSPi / BT.656 (VICAP) | same as V200 | same as V200, plus differential and single-ended pin modes |
        | Video out | CVBS, BT.656, BT.1120 (1080p@30) | CVBS, BT.1120 (1080p@30) | CVBS, BT.1120 | BT.1120 (no CVBS) | BT.1120 (no CVBS) | PAL/NTSC CVBS, BT.656, 6-bit RGB565 LCD | BT.656, RGB565 LCD (no CVBS) | - | - | - |
        | Ethernet | GMAC 10/100/1000, RGMII/MII | MAC 10/100, RGMII/MII | MAC 10/100, RGMII/MII | MAC 10/100, RGMII/MII | MAC 10/100, RMII/MII | MAC 10/100 RMII, TSO | MAC 10/100 RMII, TSO | MAC + internal FE PHY | MAC + internal FE PHY | MAC + internal FE PHY |
        | USB | 2 x USB 2.0 host | 1 x USB 2.0 host | 1 x USB 2.0 host | 1 x USB 2.0 host | 1 x USB 2.0 host | 1 x USB 2.0 host/device | 1 x USB 2.0 host/device | USB 2.0 host/device | USB 2.0 host/device | USB 2.0 host/device |
        | SDIO/MMC | 2 x MMC (SD/SDIO/eMMC) | 1 x SDIO 2.0 | 1 x SDIO 2.0 | 1 x SDIO 2.0 | 1 x SDIO 2.0 | 3 x SDIO 2.0 (two with 3.3/1.8 V) + eMMC 4.5 | 3 x SDIO 2.0 + eMMC 4.5 | 2 x SDIO + eMMC | 2 x SDIO + eMMC | 2 x SDIO + eMMC |
        | Package | FC-CSP 416, 15x15 mm, 0.65 mm | FCBGA 293, 13x13x1.37 mm, 0.65 mm | FCBGA 293, 13x13x1.37 mm, 0.65 mm | ePad QFP, 20x20x1.0 mm, 0.4 mm | BGA 220, 11x11 mm, 0.65 mm | TFBGA 273, 12x12 mm, 0.65 mm | TFBGA 231, 10x14 mm, 0.65 mm | TFBGA 192, 10x10 mm | TFBGA 192, 10x10 mm | TFBGA 273, 12x12 mm |
        | Typical power | 1200 mW | 850 mW | 700 mW | 700 mW (one value for the Hi3518 sheet) | 900 mW | 550 mW (1080p30) | 600 mW (1080p20) | - | - | - |
        | Core / DDR voltage | 1.0 V core; 1.8/1.5 V DDR; 2.5 V, 3.3 V | 1.2 V; 1.5/1.8 V DDR; 3.3 V I/O | 1.2 V; 1.5/1.8 V DDR; 3.3 V I/O | 1.2 V; 1.5/1.8 V DDR; 3.3 V I/O | 1.2 V; 1.8 V embedded DDR; 3.3 V I/O | 0.9 V; 1.5/1.35 V DDR; 3.3 V I/O | 0.9 V; 1.8 V DDR; 3.3 V I/O | - | - | - |
        | Chip ID (SC_SYSID) | 0x3516_0100 | 0x3518_0100 (as printed in the sheet) | 0x3518_0100 | 0x3518_0100 | 0x3518_0100 (as printed) | 0x3516_C300 | 0x3516_C300 (one value printed for both) | 0x3518E200, SCSYSID0[31:24] = 0x02 | 0x3518E200, [31:24] = 0x03 | 0x3518E200, [31:24] = 0x01 |
        | SDK kernel | - | Linux 3.0.y | Linux 3.0.y | Linux 3.0.y | Linux 3.0.y | Linux 3.18 | Linux 3.18 | - | - | - |

        Differences the data sheets state: the Hi3518C has no NAND controller, no CVBS output, no 90/270 degree rotation, no autofocus, two UARTs, no SSP/IR and 128 MB maximum DDR; the Hi3516C V100 is the Hi3518A with 1080p encoding; the Hi3518E V100 is a 720p part with embedded DDR2 and no NAND controller; the Hi3516E V100 differs from the Hi3516C V300 by embedded 512 Mbit DDR, a 231-pin package, no CVBS output, no two-frame WDR and the lower encoder limit; the Hi3518E V200/V201/Hi3516C V200 differ in CPU speed, DDR, package and encoder performance (table in the root description above).

        ### Memory map notes

        * See the address table above (Table 1-4): on-chip RAM 0x04010000, BOOTROM 0x04000000, SPI flash 0x58000000, DDR 0x80000000; the register windows of CRG 0x20030000, SYS_CTRL 0x20050000, MISC 0x20120000, IO mux 0x200F0000 and DDRC 0x20110000 are shared by Hi3518E V200, V201 and Hi3516C V200.

        ### DMA request lines (data sheet Table 3-12, DMAC at 0x10060000)

        | Req | Peripheral | Req | Peripheral | Req | Peripheral | Req | Peripheral |
        |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
        | 0 | I2C0 RX | 4 | UART0 RX | 8 | UART2 RX | 12 | SSP1 RX |
        | 1 | I2C0 TX | 5 | UART0 TX | 9 | UART2 TX | 13 | SSP1 TX |
        | 2 | I2C1 RX | 6 | UART1 RX | 10 | I2C2 RX | 14 | SSP0 RX |
        | 3 | I2C1 TX | 7 | UART1 TX | 11 | I2C2 TX | 15 | SSP0 TX |

        The sheet example describes UART0 RX as request 4, matching the table. Channel priority as in the other sheets: channel 0 highest.

        ### Pin multiplexing summary (generated from the IO_CONFIG registers)

        66 one-per-pin `muxctrl_regN` registers. Alternate functions per interface, as named in the register enumerations (GPIO is always one of the choices); 1 pins have no alternate function other than GPIO. Per-pin choices are in the IO_CONFIG register pages.

        | Interface | Functions |
        |---|---|
        | Serial flash (SFC / FMC) | SFC_DEVICE_MODE, SFC_EMMC_BOOT |
        | SD / SDIO / eMMC | EMMC_DATA1-7, EMMC_DS, SDIO0_CARD_DETECT, SDIO0_CARD_POWER, SDIO0_CCLK_OUT, SDIO0_CCMD, SDIO0_CDATA0-3, SDIO0_CWPR, SDIO1_CARD_DETECT, SDIO1_CARD_POWER, SDIO1_CCLK_OUT, SDIO1_CCMD_OTHER, SDIO1_CDATA0_OTHER, SDIO1_CDATA1_OTHER, SDIO1_CDATA2_OTHER, SDIO1_CDATA3_OTHER, SDIO1_CWPR_OTHER |
        | Ethernet (MAC, MII/RMII/RGMII, MDIO, PHY clock) | EPHY_CLK, EPHY_RST, MDCK, MDIO, RMII_CLK, RMII_RXD0, RMII_RXD1, RMII_RX_DV, RMII_TXD0, RMII_TXD1, RMII_TX_EN |
        | Video input (VI / VIU) | VI_DATA9-14, VI_HS_BT1120, VI_HS_SEN, VI_VS_BT1120 |
        | Video output (VO / LCD) | VO_CLK, VO_DATA0_OTHER, VO_DATA1-7, VO_DE, VO_HS, VO_VS |
        | Sensor control | FLASH_TRIG, SENSOR_CLK, SENSOR_RSTN, SHUTTER_TRIG |
        | UART | UART1_CTSN, UART1_RTSN, UART1_RTSN_OTHER, UART1_RXD, UART1_TXD, UART1_TXD_OTHER, UART2_RXD_OTHER, UART2_TXD, UART2_TXD_OTHER |
        | SPI / SSP | SPI0_CSN, SPI0_SCLK, SPI0_SDI, SPI0_SDO, SPI1_CSN0, SPI1_CSN1, SPI1_CSN1_OTHER, SPI1_SCLK, SPI1_SDI, SPI1_SDO |
        | I2C | I2C0_SCL_OTHER, I2C0_SDA, I2C1_SCL, I2C1_SCL_OTHER, I2C1_SDA, I2C2_SCL, I2C2_SDA |
        | Audio (I2S / SIO) | I2S_BCLK_RX, I2S_BCLK_TX, I2S_MCLK, I2S_SD_RX, I2S_SD_TX, I2S_WS_TX |
        | PWM | PWM0_OTHER_VALUES, PWM1-3 |
        | IR, ADC, USB, JTAG | IR, JTAG_TCK, JTAG_TDI, JTAG_TDO, JTAG_TMS, JTAG_TRSTN, SAR_ADC_CH0-3, USB_OVRCUR, USB_PWREN |
        | Boot straps and test | BOOTROM_SEL, BOOT_SEL |
        | Other | GPIO5_4_OTHER, PMC_PWM, TEMPER_DQ_OTHER, TEST_CLK |

        ### Clocks (data sheet 3.2, Tables 3-2 to 3-6)

        Three PLLs from the XIN crystal (24 MHz), two configuration registers each: APLL PERI_CRG0/1 (programmable, feeds the ARM subsystem), VPLL PERI_CRG4/5, EPLL PERI_CRG8/9. FOUTVCO = 24 MHz x (fbdiv + frac/2^24) / refdiv, must be above 600 MHz and at most 2.4 GHz. After reset the ARM9 runs from the crystal (slow mode); the PLL may only be changed in slow mode; lock status in PERI_CRG58 bit[2:0].

        | Selection / divider | Register field |
        |---|---|
        | CPU clock source / divider / skip | PERI_CRG12 bit[8] cpu_sc_sel, bit[5:4] cpu_clk_div; PERI_CRG10 bit[17] cpuclk_loaden, bit[16:12] cpuclk_skipcfg |
        | bus clock source | PERI_CRG12 bit[0] bus_sc_sel |
        | sensor clock out | PERI_CRG11 bit[18:16] sensor_cksel; vi0_sc_sel bit[2] |
        | VDP / LCD | PERI_CRG13 hd_cksel [13:12], vo_out_cksel [14], hd_lcd_cksel [17], lcd_cksel [20]; lcd_mclk_div PERI_CRG26 [26:0] |
        | AVC, VPSS, TDE, VGS, JPGE (loaden + skip) | PERI_CRG16, 18, 22, 23, 24 |
        | FMC (SFC) | PERI_CRG48 bit[3:2] sfc_cksel |
        | SDIO0 / SDIO1 | PERI_CRG49 bit[11:10] sdxc0_cksel / bit[3:2] sdxc1_cksel |
        | PWM / UART | PERI_CRG14 bit[3:2] pwm_cksel; PERI_CRG57 bit[20:19] uart_cksel |
        | ETH | PERI_CRG59 bit[7] ethcore_cksel, bit[5:4] ethphy_cksel, bit[2] eth_rmiick_sel |

        Timer count clocks: SC_CTRL timeren0ov/1ov/2ov/3ov (bits 16, 18, 20, 22): 3 MHz clock (0) or bus clock (1) per timer (the vendor U-Boot selects the bus clock for timer 0).

        ### Reset and power

        * Reset sources (data sheet 3.1): internal POR (low pulse longer than 12 XIN cycles), global soft reset from the system controller (deasserts after at least 360 system clocks, excludes clock/test circuits and registers without soft reset), per-module soft resets from the CRG (not self-clearing).
        * Power: PMC block at 0x20270000 (temperature/voltage monitor registers in the RDL); no switchable power domain is described. Modes of the system controller: normal (APLL feeds the ARM subsystem) and slow (24 MHz crystal feeds the ARM subsystem, APLL off); PLL frequency may only be changed in slow mode, the PLL needs 0.1 ms to lock, lock status is PERI_CRG58 bit[2:0].

        ### Bus ports (system controller registers)

        | Bus | Masters | Slaves |
        |---|---|---|
        | SYS AXI | CPU (M1), AHB0 (M2), AHB1 (M3) | s1 ahb_cfg, s2 sysapb, s3 mediaapb, s4 mddrc |
        | media0 AXI | AVC (M1), VGS (M2) | (towards DDR) |
        | media1 AXI | TDE / DDRT (M1), JPGE (M2), AIAO (M3), IVE / GZIP (M4) | (towards DDR) |

        Source: MISC_CTRL registers (SYS AXI, media0 AXI, media1 AXI timeout and priority fields). The data sheets name only the bus master ports of the registers; which peripheral sits behind each AHB master port is not stated (the SYS AXI masters are arbitrated at the MDDRC slave port s4).

